
{"id":"fd6702fe-05af-4d43-8df5-9e11ff73fb72","object":"chat.completion","created":1785016527,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"from collections import defaultdict\\n\\ndef solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    required_symbols = set(case['required_symbols'])\\n    node_by_id = {node['id']: node for node in nodes}\\n    children = defaultdict(list)\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        parent = node['parent']\\n        if parent is not None:\\n            children[parent].append(node['id'])\\n    root_id = None\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        if node['parent'] is None:\\n            root_id = node['id']\\n            break\\n    retained = set(node['id'] for node in nodes)\\n    sym_counts = defaultdict(int)\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        sym_counts[node['symbol']] += 1\\n    process_ids = [node['id'] for node in nodes if node['id'] != root_id]\\n    process_ids.sort(key=lambda nid: (-node_by_id[nid]['depth'], nid))\\n    removal_order = []\\n    for nid in process_ids:\\n        node = node_by_id[nid]\\n        if not node['removable']:\\n            continue\\n        if any(child in retained for child in children.get(nid, [])):\\n            continue\\n        sym = node['symbol']\\n        if sym in required_symbols and sym_counts[sym] == 1:\\n            continue\\n        retained.remove(nid)\\n        sym_counts[sym] -= 1\\n        removal_order.append(nid)\\n    retained_node_ids = sorted(retained)\\n    return {'removed_node_ids': removal_order, 'retained_node_ids': retained_node_ids}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) based on the task: SE-PE-01. The payload contains nodes (each with id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility) and required_symbols. We need to perform a grammar-guided node reduction (like Perses). The objective: reduce the tree by removing removable nodes (utility? Not sure). But the description mentions: never remove